owing the g7 they will be limited  but if  russia not with something what it says  notwithstanding president putin saying i  believe in discussions negotiations  things are moving forward i see that  things are changing  in a few hours time we'll be talking to  president putin again together with  chancellor schultz and if despite that  he steps up the bombing he's  puts kiev kiev under siege  then we know  that further massive sanctions will have  to be taken by us  the message i want to put across to you  here is that in that case  nothing is off the table nothing is  taboo we will do  whatever we deem to be  effective  and useful  to halt russia  in its aggression  let me also say that as regards the  different packages of sanctions each  time around we've been able to bring  things together very quickly whenever  necessary and to act when necessary and  yesterday evening's a meeting  demonstrated this again the ability to  work as europeans to work with our  partners to prepare things together and  we can see the impact of these sanctions  they're having a real effect and we're  going to continue  to assess the situation  so that we can take the right decisions  at the right time in order to bring  about a change in the kremlin's position  and bring it to a state of mind that'll  make it possible we hope for there to be  a ceasefire and a  cessation of facilities as quickly as  possible  thank you very much  thank you president thank you ladies and  gentlemen

